{"asserted": "ML8 is not realizable over R, THEREFORE it is not realizable over C", "cite": "the retrodiction: exactly the shape of the JC(2) C08/C20 error, in a domain whose answer is externally known", "claim": "CM-ML8-R-EMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-ML8-BASE-EXT", "path": [["M-E1", "ALONG"]]}
{"asserted": "ML8 is not realizable over Q, THEREFORE it is not realizable over Q(sqrt(-3))", "cite": "the minimal instance: a degree-2 extension already flips it", "claim": "CM-ML8-Q-EMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-ML8-Q-BASE-EXT", "path": [["M-E1q", "ALONG"]]}
{"asserted": "ML8 is realizable over C, THEREFORE it is realizable over R", "cite": "the reversed asymmetry of BASE_EXTENSION, read the wrong way", "claim": "CM-ML8-C-NONEMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-ML8-DESCENT", "path": [["M-E1", "AGAINST"]]}
{"asserted": "the 4x4 minors of the symbolic slack matrix have an F_2-solution, THEREFORE the non-Fano matroid is realizable over F_2", "cite": "the saturation trap: NONEMPTY read AGAINST a NECESSARY_CONDITION edge", "claim": "CM-NF-UNSAT-NONEMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-NF-SKIP-SAT", "path": [["M-E4", "AGAINST"]]}
{"asserted": "the eliminated/saturated variety has a rational point, THEREFORE that point is a realization of U_3,5", "cite": "Chevalley: a point of the closure need not lift", "claim": "CM-U35-CLOSURE-NONEMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-U35-CLOSURE", "note": "Expected to grade UNSOUND_PREMISE, not UNSOUND_CONCLUSION, and the distinction is real: U_3,5 IS realizable, so the conclusion happens to hold -- but the ROUTE does not, and the specific boundary point exhibited is not a realization.  The graph holds no claim contradicting it, so the derivation reaches that grading on its own.", "path": [["M-E6", "AGAINST"]]}
{"asserted": "the non-Pappus matroid is orientable, THEREFORE it is realizable over R", "cite": "the converse of MacLane's argument", "claim": "CM-NP-ORIENTABLE", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-ORIENT-TO-REAL", "path": [["M-E3np", "AGAINST"]]}
{"asserted": "ML8 admits no orientation, THEREFORE ML8 is not realizable over R", "cite": "MacLane 1936 -- the actual published argument", "claim": "CM-ML8-NONORIENT", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-MACLANE", "note": "POSITIVE CONTROL: EMPTY travelling AGAINST a NECESSARY_CONDITION edge.  Must not be flagged.", "path": [["M-E3", "AGAINST"]]}
{"asserted": "the Fano matroid is not realizable over Q, THEREFORE it is not realizable over C", "cite": "G-FANO-Q-EMPTY: 1 lies in the ideal over Q, hence over every field containing Q", "claim": "CM-FANO-Q-EMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-FANO-CONTRAST", "note": "THE CONTRAST PAIR.  Same edge type, same direction, same claim kind, an emptiness ALSO computed over a small field -- and it is LICENSED, because its certificate base-changes.", "path": [["M-E5", "ALONG"]]}
{"asserted": "ML8 is realizable over Q(sqrt(-3)), THEREFORE it is realizable over C", "cite": "a Q(sqrt(-3))-point IS a C-point", "claim": "CM-ML8-QS-NONEMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-ML8-ASCEND", "note": "POSITIVE CONTROL for the REVERSED ASYMMETRY: on the very same edge type that refuses EMPTY along the arrow, NONEMPTY passes freely.  Both halves of the asymmetry are exercised on ML8.", "path": [["M-E1c", "ALONG"]]}
{"asserted": "the frame-normalised system has a solution, THEREFORE ML8 has a realization", "cite": "G-ML8-C-WITNESS lifts the normalised solution explicitly", "claim": "CM-ML8-NORM-C", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-ML8-UP", "note": "THE SHARP CONTROL.  NONEMPTY read AGAINST the arrow is FORBIDDEN on a NECESSARY_CONDITION edge and licensed only because frame normalisation is a genuine EQUIVALENCE.", "path": [["M-E2", "AGAINST"]]}
{"asserted": "rank <= 3 holds on every realization, THEREFORE it holds on the whole closure -- which is WHY the slack ideal may be generated by the 4x4 minors", "cite": "G-U35-RANK-EXTENDS: rank 3 at the boundary point too", "claim": "CM-U35-RANK", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-U35-RANK", "note": "POSITIVE CONTROL for IMAGE_CLOSURE's one conditional cell.  A Zariski-CLOSED predicate extends to the closure; this is why elimination is a sound way to DERIVE equations even though it is unsound as a source of witnesses.", "path": [["M-E6", "ALONG"]]}
{"asserted": "the UNSATURATED ideal is already empty, THEREFORE the matroid is not realizable -- no saturation needed", "cite": "G-FANO-Q-NO-SAT", "claim": "CM-FANO-UNSAT-EMPTY", "era": "matroid", "ev": "inference", "id": "IM-FANO-NO-SAT", "note": "POSITIVE CONTROL, and the useful corollary: emptiness DOES travel against the saturation edge, so a non-realizability certificate may skip the saturation.  A witness may not.  NOTE: routed over M-E4f, the FANO saturation edge; matroid_transfer.py routed it over the non-Fano edge M-E4, which is not a connected path.", "path": [["M-E4f", "AGAINST"]]}
